<title>FRANCE: Lagardere cancels Thomson-CSF bond issue.</title>
<headline>Lagardere cancels Thomson-CSF bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lagardere SCA said on Wednesday it would not proceed with the planned issue of 5.5 billion francs in special bonds guaranteed by Credit Lyonnais and Kleinwort Benson now that the government had cancelled the sale of a 58-percent stake in Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Lagardere had lined up the financing to support its bid for the stake. The bonds would have been paid back in Thomson-CSF shares.</p>
<p>The French government on Friday decided not to continue with the privatisation programme of Thomson-CSF, a project started by the previous conservative government.</p>
</text>
